openvino_bevfusion: export the Swin backbone without 5-D tensors.

The camera encoder spent more GPU time moving data than computing: of its
25 ms on an Intel Arc Pro B60, about 11 ms were permute and reorder kernels.
Each window attention split qkv with reshape(B, N, 3, heads, d) +
permute(2, 0, 3, 1, 4) and three selects, and added the shifted-window mask
through a 5-D view; the OpenVINO GPU plugin runs both through reference
kernels. PatchMerging permuted to B, C, H, W and back.

Compute q, k and v with three Linears over the row blocks of the qkv weight,
keep the mask add 4-D by merging the head and query dimensions, and build
PatchMerging's mmcv channel order channels-last. Every value is computed by
the same operations as before: the exported camera encoder's outputs are
bit-identical, on the CPU in PyTorch and on the GPU in f16, and it takes
about 16 ms instead of 25 ms.

Remove this patch once openvino_contrib carries an equivalent change.

